{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/86228-trouble-understanding-aetheric-bleed","id":86228,"title":"Trouble understanding Aetheric Bleed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-07T13:40:58-08:00","id":86228,"title":"Trouble understanding Aetheric Bleed","content":"After reading the Aetheric Bleed condition I'm having a hard time understanding how it works. The books description: Aetheric Bleed The demon has overexerted herself to the point of exhaustion. She can no longer manage her use of Aether and it begins to pour out of her. Every turn the demon loses one Aether for every two Primum she has, round down. The demon always loses at least one Aether per turn. Causing the Condition: This Condition is the result of the demon cycling through Aether too fast. If the demon spends all of her Aether more than twice in a scene, she begins to bleed Aether as opposed to retaining it. This Condition can also be caused by failing a compromise while in demonic form. Note that this only applies after the demon is already in demonic form. Ending the Condition: The Condition ends when the demon runs out of Aether completely, when she harvests Aether from Infrastructure, or when she leaves demonic form. The player takes a Beat. Basically the cause is spending all your aether twice in a scene. If I'm understanding the rules correctly that means when a demon (in demon form) spends all of their Aether, they would then immediately roll their primum. For example a primum 5 demon spends his last aether and then rolls and gets 2 successes they would refill 2 aether. Next turn they spend the 2 aether on whatever and then would roll primum again and let's say they get one success refilling 1 aether. Once they spend that single and last aether they would then take the aetheric bleed condition as well as rolling primum. Let's say two successes this time, but the next turn comes around and they would bleed 2 points of aether putting them at zero again, the condition would subsequently be resolved earning the demon a beat and they would roll primum earning successes in aether. The condition seems very short lived and very easy to keep gaining and resolving for a lot of beats. Can anyone explain what I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2460-tazar-yoot","name":"Tazar Yoot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:58:55-08:00","id":86245,"title":"","content":"Hunted, as a Condition, is not something you want to risk, and failing compromise rolls repeatedly (by, say, spending truckloads of Aether on Exploits and demonic form powers) is going to shred your Cover to the point where you are liable to get Burned and consequently persistently Hunted.<br /> <br /> Also the roll results of Primum at 0 Aether are unlikely to result in significant returns - this goes double for when you've hit Primum 7+ and have a markedly higher Aether capacity than usual.<br /> <br /> Also also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core, pg 287, &quot;Criteria for Beats&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some rolls and powers may impart Conditions on your character. Each Condition has criteria for resolution, usually requiring a difficult choice for the character. If resolved, take a Beat. <b>You may only take one Beat for a Condition in a given scene.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:37:00-08:00","id":86276,"title":"","content":"Okay so the beat can only be earned once a scene, that's good to know. But I still fail to see the true intention of the condition because when spend your last point you'll typically regen a trivial number of aether, one or two points which would then subsequently bleed away in a turn or two resolving the condition within seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2460-tazar-yoot","name":"Tazar Yoot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T15:43:36-07:00","id":97806,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree it does not seem like the most notice-able of conditions...<br /> <br /> I guess you have to view it separately depending on what caused it. If it was caused by a compromise roll then it is actually a fairly negative condition because it would quite quickly drain your pool and if your Primum is low the replacement will be meager.<br /> <br /> The real question, as you say, is what's the point of the &quot;double-drain trigger&quot;. I am not sure but I suppose if you are a high Primum demon and you used your Aether *twice* in your demonic form in one scene then it's probably a major problem you are dealing with. A rank 5 angel or something. If that's the case then I can imagine that even the few turns of delay that the Aether Bleed will cause can be quite problematic. Though it does seem like a bit of a corner case scenario....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}